{"name":"Tulle","hex":"#f1ba91","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Tulle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town, the capital of Corrèze department, Nouvelle-Aquitaine, France."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Tulle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tulle (netting)","blocks":[{"text":"Tulle is a form of netting that is made of small-gauge thread, netted in a hexagonal pattern with small openings, and frequently starched to provide body or stiffness. It is a finer textile than the textile referred to as \"net\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Stoffballen1_%28fcm%29.jpg/330px-Stoffballen1_%28fcm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulle_(netting)","wikidata":"Q646051"},{"title":"Tulle, France","blocks":[{"text":"Tulle is a commune in central France. It is the prefecture and the second-largest town of the department of Corrèze, in the region of Nouvelle-Aquitaine. Tulle is also the episcopal see of the Roman Catholic Diocese of Tulle."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Tulle_Pr%C3%A9fecture.jpg/330px-Tulle_Pr%C3%A9fecture.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tulle%2C_France","wikidata":"Q157713"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Blue_nylon_ball_gown_2007.154.jpg/330px-Blue_nylon_ball_gown_2007.154.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Blue_nylon_ball_gown_2007.154.jpg/330px-Blue_nylon_ball_gown_2007.154.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tulle is often used to make gowns.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlue_nylon_ball_gown_2007.154.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/